  "comment": "VP-5 combat feedback (D-750): the numbers the web's combat presentation plays with, read off cehinds/ashenspire b8cfe4fac and nothing else. Every length is a CSS px, which is a Unity reference px (the web runs 1280x720 at zoom 1.5, tokens.json webSource.unityScale); every time is ms. Tracks are the web's @keyframes as stops (t is the share of the duration; a property a stop omits is interpolated between the stops that name it, as CSS does; ease names a cubic-bezier in 'easings'). 'pace' is src/ui/animationPace.js, 'feel' src/content/combatFeel.js, 'float' src/ui/fx.js floatNum and styles/combat.css, 'callout' src/ui/fx.js callout, 'effects' src/ui/combatEffectSprites.js with content/config/ui/presentation/combatEffectPlayback.json and combatEffectPresentation.json, src/content/combatDefenseEffects.js; 'poses' src/ui/enemyStates.js, src/content/enemyStateArt.js, defeatedArt.js. Read through FeedbackDefs (Application/Ui); the colours and sizes the USS draws are in ui/tokens.json (group fx*).",
